  "query_preview": "(Saturday night through Wednesday)...\nA low pressure system moving inland through central and southern\nCalifornia during the weekend will bring a chance of showers for \nSaturday through early Sunday with the most likely time for \nprecipitation Saturday night with rainfall from the coast to the\nmountains ranging from less than one-tenth inch to around one-\nquarter inch.\n\nNot much changes in winds and high temperatures is expected for \nSunday, then dry on Monday with weaker winds and with high \ntemperatures 5 to 10 degrees warmer for inland areas. Toward the \nmiddle of next week, another low pressure system could bring a \nchance of precipitation.",
